TASK B2 – Engineer an Adversarial Input: Same Size, Very Different Search (5 Marks)
Programming Language: Python
1. Aim
To design two graphs having the same number of vertices and the same number of available colours, but requiring different amounts of computational effort when solved using the backtracking graph colouring algorithm.

The objective is to demonstrate that the structure of a graph can significantly affect the performance of a backtracking algorithm.
2. Graph Design
We create two graphs with:
- Number of vertices = 10
- Number of colours (M) = 2
- Same backtracking algorithm.
- Same original vertex input order.
Graph A – Easy Graph
Colourable
