Why is Graph B difficult?

The algorithm first assigns colours to seven isolated vertices. These vertices do not create conflicts.

However, after exploring these assignments, it reaches the triangle. The triangle cannot be coloured using only two colours.

Therefore, the algorithm must backtrack and try other assignments for the seven isolated vertices before it can conclude that no solution exists.
