This demonstrates that a good vertex ordering can expose conflicts earlier and dramatically reduce unnecessary searching.
9. Result
The adversarial input experiment was successfully performed using two graphs having the same number of vertices and the same number of colours.

Graph A required very little searching because it contained no edges. Graph B required significantly more searching because the triangle conflict was placed after seven isolated vertices.

The experiment proves that the computational effort of a backtracking algorithm depends not only on input size but also on the structure of the input and the order in which decisions are made.
